{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WRFWeselyDepositionVelocity",
    "description": "Deposition velocity of WRF-Chem's Wesely scheme: SUBROUTINE depvel, the surface-resistance addition in landusevg, and SUBROUTINE cellvg (chem/module_dep_simple.F, WRF v4.8.0), for every gas on the species axis `spc` at once.\n\nSPECIES AXIS (2026-11-12). The meteorology (ustar, rmol, z0, dz1) and everything built from it alone -- the stability function, Ra and cellvg's integral -- are shared by every gas, exactly as depvel computes them once per column; only the gas index `igas` and its surface resistance `srfres` are per-species, and with them Rb, vg_max, vg_ref, vd and k_dep. The per-species equations are written as plain arithmetic on the [spc] arrays (name-aligned broadcast, esm-spec 4.3.4), so they read as the one-gas formulas they are. A consumer binds NSPEC at the mount edge to the number of deposited gases and supplies `igas` (WRF p_* slots) and `srfres` (WRFWeselySurfaceResistance.srfres, gas by gas) as [spc] arrays; this component's own tests use NSPEC = 6.\n\nThree things here are where a reimplementation of this scheme most easily goes wrong, and all three are pinned by the tests.\n\n(1) Ra is the integrated Businger HEAT profile with the turbulent Prandtl number 0.74 in front, coefficient 9 in the unstable branch, and NO arctan term -- not the momentum function. Dropping the 0.74 alone inflates Ra by 35 percent, and using the momentum form (coefficient 15, log plus arctan) adds more.\n\n(2) The reference height is 2 m, fixed, not the first layer's mid-point.\n\n(3) cellvg then converts that 2 m velocity to a LAYER MEAN over the first model layer, and it is the layer mean that WRF deposits with. Measured at the reference column, skipping cellvg overstates vd by 19 percent for HNO3, 18 percent for N2O5 and 25 percent for OH. It is the single largest structural error available here, and it is independent of every resistance difference.\n\nRb uses (Sc/Pr)^(2/3) with Pr = 0.72 -- the value the CODE uses, not the Pr = 1.0 its own stale comment claims (FORTRAN_BUGS B6), a constant factor of 1.2445.\n\nFor the tendency: `vd` and `surface_flux_coeff` are the deposition velocity and the coefficient of the surface flux boundary condition F = -vd C; `k_dep` = vd/dz1 is the first-order loss rate that implies for the first layer. WRF does not apply k_dep explicitly -- module_vertmx_wrf.F puts vd/dz1 into a theta-weighted implicit row (0.25 explicit, 0.75 implicit) and solves it simultaneously with vertical diffusion -- so k_dep is the continuous rate that discretisation approximates. dz1 is ONE parameter serving both cellvg's cell height and the tendency's layer thickness, deliberately: they are the same layer, and a component that takes them independently lets a consumer make them disagree."
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NSPEC": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 6,
      "description": "Length of the species axis `spc`: the gases this instance deposits. Bound at the mount edge by a consumer (the chem_opt = 170 column deposits every CBM-Z gas Wesely covers); 6 in this component's own tests, which is the gas set of the ESM_SWEEP regimes, and the 42 gases of each in-model call are split into seven tests of six."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "spc": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NSPEC"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "WRFWeselyDepositionVelocity": {
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": {
          "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
        },
        "dat": {
          "ref": "./wesely_data.esm"
        },
        "par": {
          "ref": "./wesely_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "igas": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 6.0,
          "description": "WRF gas index p_* (chem_opt = 101 numbering, the slot of wesely_data's tables) of each species on the axis; selects scpr23.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "srfres": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s/m",
          "default": 100.0,
          "description": "Surface resistance Rc of each gas on the axis, from WRFWeselySurfaceResistance.srfres. Supplied rather than recomputed so the two halves of the scheme stay separable.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "ustar": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 0.45,
          "description": "Friction velocity, WRF's ust(i,j)."
        },
        "rmol_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Reciprocal Monin-Obukhov length, WRF's rmol(i,j). Negative unstable, positive stable."
        },
        "z0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0.05,
          "description": "Roughness length, WRF's znt(i,j)."
        },
        "dz1": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 51.0,
          "description": "Thickness of the FIRST model layer, z_at_w(kts+1)-z_at_w(kts). It is both the cell height cellvg averages over and the layer thickness the tendency divides by -- ONE parameter for both, deliberately, because they are the same layer. The AtmosphericDeposition.jl-derived component takes the two independently (a mid-point height z and a layer pressure thickness del_P) and a consumer can silently make them disagree."
        },
        "scpr23": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "(Sc/Pr)^(2/3) of each gas on the axis, with Pr = 0.72.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "rmol": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/m",
          "description": "Reciprocal Monin-Obukhov length after depvel's neutral dead-band."
        },
        "ar": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Businger heat variable at the reference height."
        },
        "ao": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Businger heat variable at the roughness length."
        },
        "polint_unstable": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Integrated stability function, unstable branch."
        },
        "polint_neutral": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Integrated stability function, neutral branch, 0.74 ln(zr/z0)."
        },
        "polint_stable": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Integrated stability function, stable branch."
        },
        "polint": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Integrated stability function actually used. NOTE the 0.74: it is the Businger HEAT function with coefficient 9 and NO arctan term, not the momentum function. Omitting the 0.74 alone inflates Ra by 35 percent."
        },
        "aer_res": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Aerodynamic resistance as WRF reports it in aer_res_def, polint/(karman max(ustar,1e-4)). The u* floor is WRF's."
        },
        "ra": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Aerodynamic resistance between the surface and the 2 m reference height, without the u* floor."
        },
        "rb": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Quasi-laminar sublayer resistance, 2 scpr23/(karman ustar) = 5 scpr23/ustar.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "vg_max": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Deposition velocity in the absence of any surface resistance, 1/(Ra+Rb); WRF's depv.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "vg_ref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Deposition velocity AT THE 2 m REFERENCE HEIGHT, 1/(Ra+Rb+Rc).",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "pdz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "cellvg's sqrt(1-9 dz rmol)."
        },
        "pzr": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "cellvg's sqrt(1-9 zr rmol)."
        },
        "cell_fac": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "cellvg's log argument."
        },
        "a_unstable": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "cellvg's integral, unstable branch."
        },
        "a_neutral": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "cellvg's integral, neutral branch."
        },
        "a_stable": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "cellvg's integral, stable branch."
        },
        "a_cell": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "cellvg's integral actually used."
        },
        "vd": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "CELL-AVERAGED deposition velocity over the first model layer -- what WRF stores in ddvel and hands the vertical-diffusion solver. It is NOT 1/(Ra+Rb+Rc): cellvg converts the 2 m value to a layer mean, and at the reference column that is a 19 percent reduction for HNO3, 18 percent for N2O5 and 25 percent for OH. Omitting cellvg is the single largest structural error in a reimplementation of this scheme, independent of every resistance difference.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "surface_flux_coeff": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Coefficient of the downward surface flux boundary condition, F = -vd C evaluated at the first model layer. Exposed separately from k_dep so a consumer that solves the vertical-diffusion column can apply it as the boundary condition WRF applies it as, rather than as a bulk loss.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "k_dep": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "description": "First-order loss rate the surface flux implies for the first layer, vd/dz1. WRF does NOT apply this explicitly: module_vertmx_wrf.F puts vd rho b_coeff = vd/dz1 into a theta-weighted implicit row (alfa = 0.25 explicit, beta = 0.75 implicit) and solves it SIMULTANEOUSLY with vertical diffusion, so a single step is C_new = C_old (1 - 0.25 vd dt/dz1)/(1 + 0.75 vd dt/dz1) with turbulence off. k_dep is the continuous rate that discretisation approximates, and is the right thing for a consumer computing an instantaneous tendency.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        }
      },
