      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "wesely_vd_call3_part1",
          "description": "Reference: the WRF-Chem 4.8 em_scm_xy run (chem_opt = 101 RADM2 KPP) with gas_drydep_opt = 1 (data/eqwefic/chem_scm_dep; the chem_scm reference has it OFF and yields no dry-deposition truth at all). GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4 build; dumped by the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem, in wesely_driver after landusevg at call 3 (ustar 0.5892 m/s, rmol -0.01188 1/m, z0 0.050 m, first layer 51.20 m). Gas slots 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 on the species axis, in that order; Rc is taken from the same dump so this test isolates the Ra/Rb/cellvg chain. Expected value is ddvel0d, the CELL-AVERAGED velocity WRF hands the vertical-diffusion solver. Gas slot 3 (sulf) is excluded: it takes the particle path through deppart, which this component does not implement. Single-precision reference, rel 1e-5. Also asserts aer_res at this call: Same run and call 3: the aerodynamic resistance WRF reports in aer_res_def, polint/(karman max(ustar,1e-4)), which pins the stability function on its own.",
          "parameter_overrides": {
            "ustar": 0.5892362594604492,
            "rmol_in": -0.011878129094839096,
            "z0": 0.05000000074505806,
            "dz1": 51.202232360839844,
            "igas": [
              2.0,
              4.0,
              5.0,
              6.0,
              7.0,
              8.0
            ],
            "srfres": [
              2401.579833984375,
              1183.732177734375,
              5923855872.0,
              186.16810607910156,
              1.0,
              159.20587158203125
